# rp2350_lcd_154

A Waveshare RP2350-LCD-1.54, SKU 34335, or RP2350-LCD-1.54-EN, SKU 34334: an
RP2350A with 16MB of flash carrying a 240 by 240 IPS panel on an ST7789 over
four-wire SPI, a QMI8658 inertial sensor, and an ES8311 codec with an analog
microphone and an NS4150B amplifier driving a speaker. It has no touch
controller. The -EN option names the battery bundle, not the board, so both
SKUs are this one board.

It derives from pico2-arm because that is what it is: the same RP2350A the
Pico SDK configures as pico2. The SDK publishes no board header for this
product, and Waveshare's own firmware selects PICO_BOARD pico2 and drives
every peripheral by explicit GPIO number, which is exactly what deriving does
here. rp2350_touch_lcd_154 derives from this board and adds its touch
controller, so the common wiring is written once.

The panel is on SPI1: CS GP9, clock GP10, data GP11, DC GP12, backlight GP13,
reset GP14. The codec, the IMU at 0x6b, and on the touch model the touch
controller share I2C1 on GP6 and GP7. The codec's I2S link is data out GP1,
data in GP2, bit clock GP4, and word clock GP5; GP3 is its MCLK input, held
low because the codec takes its master clock from the bit clock, and GP0
enables the amplifier. GP28 is the battery enable and GP29 the battery sense
on ADC3; GP24 and GP25 are the power and volume buttons; GP18 to GP23 are the
microSD socket; GP17 is the charge status. GP26 and GP27 are the exposed UART.

Two of pico2's defaults are wrong here, and the Pico bridge's board table
replaces them for every board in this chain: GP25 is a button, not an LED, so
the board reports no LED, and the default UART's GP0 and GP1 are the
amplifier enable and the codec's playback data, so the default UART is UART1
on the exposed GP26 and GP27. ADC_AVDD is the 3V3 rail, so the ADC reference
is 3300 mV.

Nothing here drives GP28. Waveshare's firmware raises it at startup to hold
the board on when running from its battery; a program that must run on
battery does the same.

The wiring is taken from the schematic titled RP2350-Touch-LCD-1.54, which is
the only one published for the family; the non-touch board's population is
assumed to match it except for the touch controller. None of it is qualified on
hardware.

https://www.waveshare.com/product/rp2350-lcd-1.54.htm
